    {
      "kind_id": "mini.pair-proposal.grid.v1",
      "title": "Proposal: a grid cell",
      "input_ports": [
        {
          "port_id": "problem",
          "port_type": "problem",
          "window": "all"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "rules",
          "port_type": "kernel_rules",
          "window": "this_cycle"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "earlier",
          "port_type": "pair_proposals",
          "window": "all"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "verdicts",
          "port_type": "earlier_verdicts",
          "window": "all"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "criticisms",
          "port_type": "criticisms",
          "window": "previous_cycle"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "executions",
          "port_type": "pair_executions",
          "window": "all"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "catalogue",
          "port_type": "evidence_legend",
          "window": "all",
          "params": {
            "tiers": [
              "evidence"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "output_port": {
        "port_id": "out",
        "produces_kind": "mini.pair-proposal.grid.v1"
      },
      "instruction": "You are shown the documented rules of the recovery check, not its code. The inputs of interest are replies built from three kinds of part: a JSON object, prose, and a code fence (``` lines). The grid of shapes: where the object stands (inside a fence, outside a fence, both), where prose stands (before the object, after it, inside the fence before the object, inside the fence after it, between two objects), and how many objects there are (one, two: the same, two: different). Each proposal covers ONE cell of that grid that no earlier proposal covered, named in the commitments as 'cell'. Write the input as a reply of that shape, the rewritten text as the same reply with ONE part moved or added, and say what the rule says the recovered object ought to do: move or stay. Your expectation comes from the rule's words alone. The commitments are a STRING whose content is JSON of the form {\"kernel\": \"<id>\", \"input\": \"<the input text>\", \"rewritten\": \"<your rewritten text>\", \"expect\": \"moves\" or \"unchanged\", \"rewrite\": \"<one sentence naming what you changed>\"}. The input and the rewritten text are instances written out in full, never descriptions. Do not repeat a pair shown among the earlier proposals. The commitments also carry \"cell\": \"<the cell, in words>\".",
      "format": {
        "commitments": {
          "all_of": [
            {
              "check": "json_schema",
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "kernel",
                  "input",
                  "rewritten",
                  "expect",
                  "rewrite",
                  "cell"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "kernel": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "pattern": "^conformance\\.kernel\\.(recovery|recovered-from-prose|response-verdict)$"
                  },
                  "input": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "minLength": 1
                  },
                  "rewritten": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "minLength": 1
                  },
                  "expect": {
                    "enum": [
                      "moves",
                      "unchanged"
                    ]
                  },
                  "rewrite": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "minLength": 3
                  },
                  "cell": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "minLength": 3
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "commitment_call": "single"
    },
    {
      "kind_id": "mini.pair-execution.v1",
      "title": "Execution",
      "input_ports": [
        {
          "port_id": "proposals",
          "port_type": "pair_proposals",
          "window": "this_cycle"
        }
      ],
      "output_port": {
        "port_id": "out",
        "produces_kind": "mini.pair-execution.v1"
      }
    },
    {
